  "title": "An Exact Certificate for the (n,k) = (4,3) Monomial Lie-Additive Diameter",
  "batch_label": "51",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For V=Sym^3(C^4), U=Sym^3(span(e_1,e_2,e_3)), and rho(X)=sum_{i,j} x_ij e_i partial/partial(e_j), there exist m_1,m_2 in mon(rho(sl_4(C))) with m_1 U+m_2 U=V; hence the monomial Lie-additive diameter in the frozen (n,k)=(4,3) cell is exactly 2. Specifically, m_1 is the identity and m_2=rho(X_1)rho(X_2)rho(X_3) for the three explicit traceless integer matrices in evidence/resolution_argument.md, with X_3 acting first.",
